1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,240
That ball's going out.

2
00:00:01,470 --> 00:00:04,214
The model called it 325 milliseconds early.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,530
Our computer vision calls the point before the ball lands,

4
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:10,621
so we trade the Polymarket match price before it reprices.

5
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,990
Polymarket prices each match from zero to a dollar,

6
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:15,470
a player's chance to win,

7
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:17,970
and reprices about a second after each point.

8
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:20,235
The fastest traders won eleven months of eleven.

9
00:00:21,483 --> 00:00:22,153
Think it's a gimmick?

10
00:00:22,383 --> 00:00:24,533
Watch it call misses on real games it never saw.

11
00:00:24,763 --> 00:00:27,373
A miss call means it knows the ball is out before it lands.

12
00:00:27,593 --> 00:00:29,443
Not one was made on a ball labelled in.

13
00:00:34,033 --> 00:00:35,899
Real tennis, with our tennis tracker.

14
00:00:37,933 --> 00:00:40,923
Add spin: landing error drops five to eight times.

15
00:00:41,153 --> 00:00:43,838
Out, called 200 milliseconds before the bounce.

16
00:00:45,533 --> 00:00:47,473
Here's the whole pipeline in milliseconds:

17
00:00:47,703 --> 00:00:49,143
our part, about fifty.

18
00:00:49,373 --> 00:00:54,871
Add a one-second feed and Polymarket's one-second delay: 2.1 seconds. Under three.

19
00:00:55,567 --> 00:00:56,567
Here's what speed is worth:

20
00:00:56,797 --> 00:00:57,927
every second costs money;

21
00:00:58,167 --> 00:01:00,137
by three seconds, every version loses.

22
00:01:00,347 --> 00:01:01,716
The edge halves within a second.

23
00:01:03,617 --> 00:01:05,277
The test: months of backtest.

24
00:01:05,497 --> 00:01:08,327
One match: dots are paper trades on the real price.

25
00:01:08,557 --> 00:01:10,766
59 percent of traded matches made money.

26
00:01:13,167 --> 00:01:15,727
And the profit, at a simulated one-second feed,

27
00:01:15,957 --> 00:01:16,907
post-hoc estimate:

28
00:01:17,087 --> 00:01:19,377
94 dollars a day, Sharpe 12:

29
00:01:19,607 --> 00:01:22,557
return per unit of risk, above two is very good.

30
00:01:22,787 --> 00:01:25,427
On data it never saw: 57 a day.

31
00:01:26,233 --> 00:01:27,849
Courtside. Paper trading only.
